      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/polygon/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>mr.ramzan.bhutto@gmail.com (Muhammad Ramzan)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/polygon/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;why-polygon&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Why Polygon?&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#why-polygon&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To prepare a problem, you need a statement, a validator, a checker, a generator, tests, and a solution to prove it&amp;rsquo;s all correct. You can hack this together with loose scripts, but it gets messy fast: how do you know a test is valid? How do you know your solution is right before you even have tests? What happens when the generator changes and everything needs to be redone?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
